WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.580
Let's talk about impeachment briefly.

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.050
Um, support for impeaching.

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:10.730
Donald Trump has spiked to 41%, but I want
to go through this carefully because there

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:14.080
are different things that impeachment could
mean.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.270
As you probably all know by now, because I
keep mentioning it, impeachment is not the

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.160
removal of the president.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:25.800
Impeachment is the process whereby the house
says we believe the president should be removed

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.550
for these reasons and we are filing articles
of impeachment.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.760
It then is up to the Senate to vote, to convict
and remove the president.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.360
And these are two different processes and
a lot of people are interchangeably using

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:44.470
the word impeachment to mean either started
impeachment inquiry, file articles of impeachment

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:49.440
in the House, go through the investigative
process of impeachment in the House and actually

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.620
vote to remove Trump in the senate.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.220
But those are for different things.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.220
Okay.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:59.740
There's a new CNN poll conducted by SSRS,
which says that 41% of the country now wants

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.060
Donald Trump impeached and removed from office.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.600
It's good that they're asking the question
in that way.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.290
Now this is actually not the record high for
Donald Trump's presidency.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:15.800
The same pole back in September had 47% of
the country wanting Trump impeached in December.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:22.080
43% of the country wanted Donald Trump impeached
and removed, and it dropped into the mid thirties

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:27.200
and now it's back up to 41% the most important
takeaway is that this is a lot.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:32.390
It's not normal that 41% of the country wants
the president to be impeached and removed,

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:38.170
and not surprisingly, the recent rise in those
numbers is driven primarily by Democrats and

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:40.670
some centrist Independence Democrats.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:44.070
Now, 76% support impeaching Donald Trump.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.930
That's up eight points from April, so this
tells us a few important things.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:52.650
Number one, it's just not normal for more
than 40% of the country to believe the president

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:53.760
should be impeached.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:58.900
Even during the hyperpartisan and sanity of
the Obama Administration, the highest impeachment

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:06.300
support ever for Barack Obama was 33% even
for Bill Clinton who was impeached, impeachment

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:13.731
support never surpassed 30% if I recall correctly,
the current president has 41% impeachment

00:02:13.731 --> 00:02:15.190
and removal support.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:16.790
That is massive.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:22.790
Number two, support for impeachment, especially
among Democrats and independents, seems to

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:27.920
be correlated with the number of prominent
Democratic lawmakers who are calling for impeachment

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:28.920
proceedings.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:34.810
Now, we don't know for sure if national support
for impeachment is going up because more prominent

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:36.310
Democrats are calling for impeachment.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:41.590
I don't know if more prominent Democrats are
calling for impeachment because they see that

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:45.360
more Americans are supporting it, so I don't
know about which way the causation goes, if

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.790
any, but it's a trend that's rising in parallel.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:49.990
They're correlated.

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:54.310
At least this is the most important thing
to understand here.

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:59.970
Do not let the Trump administration and right
wing media trick you into believing that it's

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:03.550
no big deal that 41% of the country wants
Trump impeached.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:08.350
Impeachment of a president of the United States
has happened only I believe three times in

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:13.900
the more than 240 years that the United States
has been a country.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:19.730
That 41% support doing that is rare.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:25.349
And I believe that as more facts come out,
if more Americans read the Mueller report,

00:03:25.349 --> 00:03:30.489
if an impeachment inquiry starts, which Bernie
Sanders is now calling for, I'll talk about

00:03:30.489 --> 00:03:31.710
that after the break.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.750
The 41% number is going to go up.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:38.830
And what the Trump administration is going
to insist on is this is just partisan nonsense.

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:41.670
It's partisan, bad, angry democrats.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:50.130
Once you get to 45% 47% 48% mathematically
it cannot be just partisan democrats.

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:53.910
So do not let them trick you into thinking
that this is no big deal.

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:54.910
This is a big deal.

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:56.710
There've been three impeachments in American
history.

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:58.440
I hope I'm getting that number right.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:03.489
Um, and that more than 40% of the country
wants that done to the current president is

00:04:03.489 --> 00:04:05.760
a massive, massive deal.

